      "writtenOn": "2024-01-08T18:39:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From a Rust perspective, you don\u0027t need `{`-`}` as the temporary value `fdt.root().unwrap()` in\n```\nlet name \u003d fdt.root().unwrap().name();\nassert_eq!(Ok(cstr!(\"\")), name);\n```\nwould also go out of scope before the assertion.\n\nHowever, this style can be used to make clear the intent of the test.\n\nTherefore, would you mind adding a comment (e.g. at the end) of each seemingly unnecessary block to document what the purpose was e.g.\n```\nlet name \u003d {\n    let root \u003d fdt.root().unwrap();\n    root.name()\n    // root goes out of scope\n};\nassert_eq!(Ok(cstr!(\"\")), name);\n```\nthis would also act similarly to a `SAFETY` comment, where we have to convince ourselves of the necessity of the block (e.g. the `{`-`}` on line 445 achieve nothing and can be removed).",
      "range": {
